{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1263249-the-crow-is-top-dollar-a-vampire","id":1263249,"title":"The Crow - Is Top Dollar a Vampire?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness"],"posts":[{"date":"2018-10-28T13:53:28-07:00","id":1263249,"title":"The Crow - Is Top Dollar a Vampire?","content":"In the 1994 movie The Crow Michael Wincott's character Top Dollar and his girlfriend Myca only appear at night or indoors. They are more clean and stylised than other characters and their dress sense is anachronistic (ish) so as a result they appear almost unearthly. They also 'go through' a couple of girls and Top dollar thrusts a sword through Skank. Later on Top dollar survives the epic gunfight apparently without a scratch and only dies when he suffers a supernatural attack, falls, and is 'impaled on the horns of a gargoyle' i.e. staked and/or severing the spine<br /> <br /> Does all of this allow for a reading of the film where Top Dollar and Myca are vampires? When thinking of them as WoD vampires Top Dollar's sense of style and obsession with burning things down could be a Toreador fascination and Myca could easily be taken for a Malkavian.<br /> <br /> <br /> Wikipedia - <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/The_Crow_(1994_film)\" target=\"_blank\">https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/The_Crow_(1994_film)</a><br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11490-dogstar","name":"Dogstar","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11490_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"381"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-10-28T15:54:58-07:00","id":1263271,"title":"","content":"I mean, if you want? But it's not part of the film (and even less part of the comics). It's just the style of the film.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-10-29T18:32:20-07:00","id":1263454,"title":"","content":"Sure. Why not? The movie cements itself as one of the inspirations behind the World of Darkness(dynamically) and I could see a number of things fitting inside a chronicle for Vampire or Wraith.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#333333\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\">&quot;Steel isn't strong, boy. Flesh is stronger.&quot;</span></span></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/95-fat-larry","name":"Fat Larry","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar95_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1337"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-10-31T12:41:21-07:00","id":1263855,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Fat Larry</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1263249-the-crow-is-top-dollar-a-vampire?p=1263454#post1263454\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The movie cements itself as one of the inspirations behind the World of Darkness(dynamically)...</div> </div> </div> </div>More the other way around, isn't it? I recall some of the graphic symbols from the original Mage game being featured in the movie. Of course back in the early-to-mid 90s White Wolf was in the thick of Goth culture, so there was probably a lot of interplay.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3505-matt-the-bruins-fan","name":"Matt the Bruins fan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3505_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2401"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-10-31T13:08:07-07:00","id":1263864,"title":"","content":"A lot of Mage's symbols come from real world sources. The Sphere icons are all from actual European alchemy symbology... so it seems more like pulling from the same sources than anything else.<br /> <br /> Of course, the Crow movie came out well after the WoD started to have a strong sense of self (1994, VtM and WtA were into their 2e, Mage and Wraith were out already for their 1e), with the Crow comics being from 1989 (two years before VtM 1e was published).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-10-31T19:24:52-07:00","id":1263955,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Matt the Bruins fan</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1263249-the-crow-is-top-dollar-a-vampire?p=1263855#post1263855\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> More the other way around, isn't it? I recall some of the graphic symbols from the original Mage game being featured in the movie. Of course back in the early-to-mid 90s White Wolf was in the thick of Goth culture, so there was probably a lot of interplay.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Eh. Many White Wolf writers cite The Crow was their inspiration behind their writing. So I was merely coming at it from that perspective. Maybe they meant the comic, too?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#333333\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\">&quot;Steel isn't strong, boy. Flesh is stronger.&quot;</span></span></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/95-fat-larry","name":"Fat Larry","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar95_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1337"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-11-01T04:40:10-07:00","id":1264002,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Fat Larry</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1263249-the-crow-is-top-dollar-a-vampire?p=1263955#post1263955\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> Eh. Many White Wolf writers cite The Crow was their inspiration behind their writing. So I was merely coming at it from that perspective. Maybe they meant the comic, too?</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Its not like the WOD sprouted fully formed in its first books, that we can even talk about Edition flavor should say that. The Crow, the Matrix, Dark City all clearly influenced writers after they came out and found references in the WOD.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2715-lian","name":"Lian","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5218"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}